---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the SOCHSE public website and planned Compass integrations."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy policy"
    description="How the SOCHSE public website and client-authorized Compass integrations handle information."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow-container prose">
      <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> 31 July 2026</p>

      <h2>Public website</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static informational website. At launch, SOCHSE does not use
        advertising cookies, behavioral tracking, or a website contact form.
        If analytics are added later, this policy will be updated before use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare delivers and protects this website and may process ordinary
        network and request information according to its own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        When you email SOCHSE, the message, address, and information you provide
        are used to respond, assess the request, and maintain appropriate
        business records. Do not send passwords, API tokens, medical
        information, financial account details, or other sensitive material in
        an initial enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>SOCHSE Compass and Google user data</h2>
      <p>
        Compass is under development. When a client explicitly enables a Google
        Ads integration, Compass may request authorized access to account,
        campaign, spend, and performance information needed for the agreed
        reporting capability.
      </p>
      <p>
        Client authorization is used only to provide and support the requested
        Compass function. SOCHSE does not sell Google user data. Each client
        installation is designed to keep its data and credentials isolated.
        Access can be revoked through the relevant Google account controls.
        Clients may request deletion of SOCHSE-controlled support records by
        contacting the address below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use and transfer of information received from Google APIs will follow
        the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
          Google API Services User Data Policy
        </a>,
        including its Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Sharing</h2>
      <p>
        SOCHSE does not sell personal information. Information may be shared
        only when needed with infrastructure or communication providers, when
        directed by the relevant client, to protect rights and systems, or when
        legally required.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        Information is retained only as long as reasonably needed for the
        stated purpose, contractual records, security, or legal obligations.
        Reasonable technical and organizational safeguards are used, but no
        internet service can promise absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask what information SOCHSE controls about you, request a
        correction or deletion where applicable, or withdraw a voluntary
        enquiry. Client integrations have separate authorization and
        offboarding procedures.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:sochsecompass@gmail.com">sochsecompass@gmail.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
